completionNarrative:
Done.

**Defect:** In `lib/asyncify.js`, the check for whether a wrapped function returned a Promise had an inverted condition:

```js
if (result && typeof result.then !== 'function') {
    return handlePromise(result, callback)
}
```

This meant non-Promise return values were passed to `handlePromise` (which calls `.then`, breaking everything), while actual Promises fell through to `callback(null, result)` — so `asyncify` of any Promise-returning function returned the raw Promise instead of invoking the callback, and `null`/`undefined` returns crashed in `handlePromise`.

**Fix:** Flipped `!==` to `===`, so Promises go through `handlePromise` and everything else is passed straight to the callback — matching the upstream async.js implementation.

**Result:** `npm run --silent test` now passes — 690 passing, 0 failing (previously 22 asyncify failures). No tests were touched; the only change is the one-character operator in `lib/asyncify.js`.
